    {
      "strategyName": "Non-NDW (Blade Boost)",
      "weather": "Extreme",
      "adventureEffect": "Blade Boost",
      "difficulty": "4★",
      "text": "<h2>Overview</h2><p>Lunala's movesets can be some problematic with access to powerful psychic  and ghost type movesets. Gengar Routes are ideally used against Moonblast and or dodging the super effective shadow ball/future sight/psychic.</p><p><strong>Estimated TTW: 280.0s-295.0s</strong></p><p><br></p><h2>Main Strategies:</h2><p>Simply DPS with Gengars, <a href=\"https://soloraidarchive.github.io/solo-raid-mechanics.html#strategy-hot-swap\" target=\"_blank\">swapping</a> to the next gengar once the active gengar is unable to continue. After all gengar's are too low to continue, heal and <a href=\"https://soloraidarchive.github.io/solo-raid-mechanics.html#strategy-rejoin\" target=\"_blank\">rejoin</a> the raid. </p><p>Vs: Shadow ball, Psychic, Future Sight: </p><p>It is entirely possible that Lunala will release a charge move after a rejoin is performed. If using the gengar strategy it is recommended to run a <a href=\"https://soloraidarchive.github.io/solo-raid-mechanics.html#strategy-substitute\" target=\"_blank\">subsitute</a> in the first slot to intercept this move if it occurs. A substitute is run in the first slot of each battle party from the first rejoin onwards. </p><p><br></p><p>Some Substitute Options: </p><ol><li data-list=\"bullet\"><span class=\"ql-ui\" contenteditable=\"false\"></span>Shadow Darkrai (any but moonblast)</li><li data-list=\"bullet\"><span class=\"ql-ui\" contenteditable=\"false\"></span>Shadow Chandelure (Any but shadow ball)</li><li data-list=\"bullet\"><span class=\"ql-ui\" contenteditable=\"false\"></span>Shadow Tyranitar (Any but moonblast) </li><li data-list=\"bullet\"><span class=\"ql-ui\" contenteditable=\"false\"></span>Mega Mewtwo Y (Any)</li></ol><p><br></p><p>More Videos coming soon: </p>",
